{
  "module": "Attention: how tokens exchange information",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "qkv-projections",
    "title": "Queries, keys and values",
    "summary": "How each token's vector is turned into three new vectors, a query, a key and a value, by three learned matrices, and what shapes they have.",
    "covers": ["qkv-projections"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "attention-gist",
        "reason": "Q, K and V are how attention is carried out."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "sequence-shapes",
        "reason": "The projections are described by their shapes, such as n × d_model."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "training-basics",
        "reason": "The three matrices are learned parameters."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "three-roles",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "To take a weighted mix, each position needs three different things: something to "
            },
            {
              "text": "look for",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " relevant positions with, something for others to "
            },
            {
              "text": "match against",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and the "
            },
            {
              "text": "content",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to contribute."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So each token's vector is turned into three new vectors: a "
            },
            {
              "text": "query",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", a "
            },
            {
              "text": "key",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and a "
            },
            {
              "text": "value",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 30)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-analogy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "text": "query",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " is what this position is looking for."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "text": "key",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " is what each position advertises, for others to match against."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "text": "value",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " is the content a position contributes if it is attended to."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This is an analogy for intuition, not a description of the mechanism. What the numbers in a query or a key mean is decided by training, and nobody writes them by hand."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 30)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "projections",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "X is the matrix of token vectors, one row per token, with shape n × d_model. Three matrices turn it into Q, K and V:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "Q = X W_Q \\qquad K = X W_K \\qquad V = X W_V",
          "spoken": "Q equals X times W Q, K equals X times W K, V equals X times W V"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each of these is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "projection",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": a matrix multiplication that turns every row of X into a row of the result."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 30)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "shapes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "W_Q and W_K have shape d_model × d_k, and W_V has shape d_model × d_v. A matrix product (a × b)(b × c) has shape a × c, so:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Q = X W_Q is n × d_k"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "K = X W_K is n × d_k"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "V = X W_V is n × d_v"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "For example, with n = 3 tokens, d_model = 4 and d_k = 2: X is 3 × 4, W_Q is 4 × 2, and Q is 3 × 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Every token has its own query, its own key and its own value: one row each."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 30)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "learned",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "W_Q, W_K and W_V are "
            },
            {
              "text": "parameters",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", learned during training like all the others. At inference they are frozen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Q, K and V are different: they are "
            },
            {
              "text": "computed from the input",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", so they change for every new text."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 30, 9)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
